Chongqing vocational schools pilot modern apprenticeship system; students become enterprise employees upon enrollment - Xinhuanet
Reporters learned from the Municipal Education Commission yesterday that from this year, the city will pilot the talent training model of "modern apprenticeship" in 60 vocational schools. Students who are accepted for pilot training will have the status of apprentices, and will be pre-registered as employees of pilot enterprises after enrollment.
The Municipal Education Commission requires that the admission and enrollment procedures of vocational schools be standardized, and the dual identity of apprentices as students of vocational schools and potential employees of enterprises be clarified. According to the principle of mutual selection, apprentices, schools, and enterprises should sign a tripartite agreement. For apprentices who are 16 years old but not yet 18, an agreement must be signed by apprentices, guardians, schools, and enterprises to determine the rights and interests of all parties and the specific positions, teaching content, and rights protection for apprentices in their jobs.
Pilot schools are encouraged to adopt the modern apprenticeship system and jointly carry out pre-job training and post-position training for enterprise employees with cooperative enterprises.
The pilot schools should reform the talent training model.
Schools and enterprises jointly design talent training programs, and jointly formulate professional teaching standards, curriculum standards, post standards, enterprise master standards, quality control standards and corresponding implementation plans.
The pilot is carried out in one cycle of training, and the internship time of students in enterprises is determined according to the professional talent training plan. The on-the-job internship is generally six months.
In the enterprise practice, the enterprise team management model should be implemented. According to the characteristics of different professions, one master can lead 2-5 apprentices to form a learning group, ensuring that students master the skills required for each training post.
According to the arrangement, from 2016 to August 2019, our city will determine 60 municipal pilot projects of modern apprenticeship in three batches, with about 50 people in each pilot project, and a total of about 3,000 students (apprentices) will be trained.
In accordance with the principle of first pilot and then implementation, and gradually promote from point to surface, we will explore and establish a long-term mechanism for joint enrollment, joint training, and integrated education between schools and enterprises, effectively improve students' post skills, and increase students' employment rate and employment quality.
