China Children's Center to Hold a Series of Activities to Let Children Celebrate "Children's Day" with "High Technology" - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 (Huang Xiaoxi, Zhou Shanshan) -- Reporters learned from the China Children's Center on May 20 that from May 28 to June 1, around Children's Day, the China Children's Center plans to hold a series of activities such as children's maker experience, children's visual art festival, and parent-child book carnival, so that children can spend Children's Day in the charm of cutting-edge technology.
It is understood that the activities held by the China Children's Center during this year's Children's Day include "Love Home, Create Cool" Children's Future Learning Carnival, the First Children's Visual Art Festival, "Book Carnival" and "All Family Loves Reading" Picture Book Series.
Li Zhongming, deputy director of the China National Children's Center, said at the media briefing for the 2016 "June 1" Children's Day held on the 20th that the "Love Home and Create Cool" Children's Future Learning Carnival is a key event for the China National Children's Center to celebrate "June 1" this year.
The event focuses on the organic integration of social innovation and family personal creativity. By involving children and families in various innovative educational activities, the innovation practice becomes the cultural gene of the masses, and “doing it yourself” becomes a new learning and living style for the masses.
It is understood that the "Love Home and Create Cool" Children's Future Learning Carnival includes the "Bean Fruit Maker" experience activities, the anniversary celebration of the Old Cow Children's Exploration Museum and the "Explore Family Love, Children Celebrate Children's Day" event, the VR public experience plan, and the "Maker Tribe" interactive workshop, as well as dozens of cutting-edge technology experience contents.
