Education commentary: What is needed to rescue abducted children?
If we compare it with the famous public welfare advertisement “no buying, no killing”, then in a good environment where there is no demand for “rescue”, the collective defense and prevention of abduction, and the nationwide anti-abduction campaign will make the abduction and sale of children unprofitable, risky and costly, and such crimes will not occur repeatedly.
Recently, the Missing Children Emergency Release Platform developed by the Anti-Abduction Office of the Criminal Investigation Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security was launched.
This is an Internet information platform created to establish an authoritative channel for releasing information on missing children and to find abducted children in time.
When I heard that the name of the app was “Reunion”, I felt very warm.
The new technology is not only named “literary and artistic” and full of sentiment, but also properly applied in information technology, practical and effective.
The primary goal of anti-abduction law enforcement is to find abducted children and protect their personal safety and freedom.
Second, there is the trial and punishment of suspects.
The meaning of criminal punishment can be listed in many “big words”, from individual punishment, social prevention to legal education.
However, before the trafficking case is solved, priority should be given to the personal safety of the victims.
There are urgent matters that cannot wait, and in the face of the urgent “rescue” goal, the controversial and disputable topics such as “whether the abduction of children should be punished with death penalty” can be put aside and discussed cautiously; but the rescue of abducted children cannot wait.
According to the experience of investigating such cases, human traffickers are accustomed to leaving the scene of the crime as soon as possible after they succeed.
Every minute of delay in the abduction operation may make the child further away from his parents, and the difficulty of solving the case will increase.
In this case, it is a pragmatic action to come up with an effective method such as the “Reunion” platform that can directly help solve cases and find children.
After all, "fighting against abduction" is a major task that requires the operation of the entire legal system.
To combat crime and protect children and parents, from the improvement of legislation to judicial protection and the meticulousness of law enforcement, we need to implement the care of "protecting young people and supporting the weak".
In addition, prevention of child trafficking can be improved from family to society.
For example, a common case is that a family of three is resting at the train station. The parents are sound asleep, and when they wake up, they find that their child is missing.
A two-year-old cannot be expected to have sufficient self-protection skills, but as a parent of a young child, you should at least have a reasonable awareness of protection.
The simplest means of protecting children from abduction is to ensure that parents take turns resting or leave their children in a safe place.
From another aspect of the police's fight against trafficking crimes, the side that purchases abducted children should also be concerned and punished.
A single act of wrongdoing is often just one link in a long chain.
According to China’s Criminal Law, the minimum sentence for child trafficking is five years; in cases of particularly serious circumstances, the death penalty may be imposed, and property confiscated.
The starting point of the sentence is high, and the maximum sentence is heavy. In the general trend of "lightening the sentence", the crime of abducting children is obviously a crime with a heavy sentence.
However, there are still many cases of human trafficking every year.
It can be seen that some people have backward ideas in raising children and weak legal awareness.
The legal education of this group should be carried out in parallel.
To effectively control trafficking crimes, it is not enough to rely on strict law enforcement by the government.
If the "market" of abduction is widespread, and the abductors are greedy for money, they will constantly innovate their methods of abduction, forming a "battle" with law enforcement officers, and the anti-abduction campaign will inevitably fall into an inefficient quagmire.
Therefore, breaking down backward thinking and popularizing legal knowledge can also help eradicate the crime of abduction and purchase of children.
Yang Haidong delivered a lecture on the spirit of the 19th CPC Sixth Plenary Session and the Provincial Party Congress in Malanshan.
Drawing strength from the Party’s century-long struggle
Hunan Daily, December 10 (All-media reporter Gong Baiwei) According to the unified arrangement of the Provincial Party Committee, Yang Haodong, member of the Standing Committee of the Provincial Party Committee and head of the Propaganda Department of the Provincial Party Committee, gave an interactive presentation in Malanshan Video Cultural and Creative Park on the morning of December 10, to thoroughly study and implement the spirit of the Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee, the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches, instructions and directives for Hunan, and the spirit of the 12th Provincial Party Congress.
Yang Haidong expounded the core essence and practical requirements of the spirit of the plenary session in a simple and comprehensive manner from three aspects, namely, ideal belief and original mission, self-revolution and youthful party, and party leaders and party theory, combined with his own feelings and personal experience.
He pointed out that we should combine the spirit of the plenary session with the spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's important speeches, instructions and directives to Hunan, and the spirit of the Provincial Party Congress, and study them thoroughly, enhance the ideological, political and action consciousness of defending the "two establishments" and achieving the "two upholds", and move forward along the direction guided by General Secretary Xi Jinping.
In the interactive exchange session, representatives of grassroots cadres, enterprises and young people asked questions on the relationship between the three historical resolutions, how to understand the decisive significance of "two establishments", how cultural enterprises should grasp the orientation, and how young people in the new era can draw strength from 100 years of party history. Yang Haodong answered these questions with simple language and vivid examples. He earnestly exhorted the young party members to draw strength from the party’s century-long struggle, unite closely around the Party Central Committee, remain firm in following the Party, and write responsibility and dedication with their youth.
It is estimated that the number of college graduates in Beijing will reach 268,000 in 2022 - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 11 (Reporter Yang Na) - The reporter learned from the video conference on employment and entrepreneurship of graduates in 2022 held recently by the Beijing Municipal Education Commission and the Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau that the number of college graduates in Beijing is expected to reach 268,000 in 2022, an increase of 16,000 over last year.
According to the relevant person in charge of Beijing Human Resources and Social Security Bureau, Beijing will deploy the employment work for college graduates from aspects such as strengthening supply and demand matching, strengthening policy support, broadening employment channels, ensuring assistance to the needy, supporting innovation and entrepreneurship, and improving service efficiency.
The reporter learned that the Beijing Municipal Human Resources and Social Security Bureau will build a practice platform, increase job supply, take the initiative to contact 40 workplace experience bases for college graduates, visit employers, and integrate demand information and job information; focus on "six batches", namely, expand the recruitment of public institutions, expand the recruitment of state-owned enterprises, expand the recruitment of grass-roots projects, expand the recruitment of conscripts, expand the employment probation and retention, and expand the entrepreneurship-driven employment; implement "one policy for one life" dynamic management, recommend no less than 5 job information for each graduate, and ensure that 100% of the graduates from poor families who are willing to work will be helped.
