Jiangxi will train 10,000 rural primary school music, physical education and art teachers within three years - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Nanchang, May 22 (Reporter Chen Yushan) The reporter learned from the Jiangxi Provincial Education Department recently that in order to strengthen the ability to guarantee the shortage of teachers in the teaching team and achieve balanced development of rural compulsory education, Jiangxi Province has planned to train one qualified music, art and physical education teacher for each primary school in the rural areas (townships and below) in the province for three years from 2016, a total of 10,000 teachers.
It is understood that this training was aimed at teachers in primary schools in rural areas of Jiangxi Province under 45 years old who have knowledge or talent in music, art and sports, and can also teach music, art and sports courses.
Through the training, they master the basic knowledge and teaching skills of music, physical education and fine arts, update their teaching ideas and concepts, master modern teaching methods, improve their ability to teach subjects, design activities, develop campus culture and self-development, build a team of music, physical education and fine arts teachers with one specialty and multiple abilities, and alleviate the problem of lack of rural music, physical education and fine arts teachers.
To ensure the quality and effectiveness of training, Jiangxi also plans to train 100 primary school music, art, and sports teachers in 100 counties (cities, districts) across the province, totaling 300 trainers, to comprehensively improve their teaching demonstration leadership, teaching research activity design and organization, training, and online workshop construction capabilities, and play a role in teaching, demonstration, guidance, and supervision.
