What will be the hottest thing in 2021?
It is undoubtedly the Tokyo Olympics.
Do you think only Olympic athletes can win awards?
A few days ago, an article titled "Look! Project managers can win gold medals in Olympic events" was very popular. It mentioned that project managers could be the first in many projects and no one could match them: moving bricks, business trips, staying up late were the daily routine of project managers; fire fighting, taking the blame, apologizing were not a problem.
A seemingly joking article reveals the daily hardships of project managers. It represents the inadequacy of current project management work.
And those who work in project management are gradually choosing to take some action to get themselves out of the dilemma in their work.
The number of PMP (internationally certified project management professional qualification) applicants has increased year on year, indicating that more and more project management practitioners are seeking to improve their project management skills through learning.
According to the “20-Year Development Report of Project Management in China (1999-2019)”, as of September 2019, the total number of PMP® applicants in China was nearly 600,000, the number of PMP® certified individuals was about 420,000, and the number of valid certificate holders was about 300,000, accounting for 31.2% of the total number of PMP® certificate holders in the world.
The number of PMP certificate holders has increased year by year in the past decade, which indicates that more and more project managers realize that it is no longer advisable to simply copy the “old experience” to do things. The ever-changing work environment tells us that we need to learn to stand on the shoulders of scientific giants to explore the way forward.
However, does obtaining a PMP certification guarantee smooth project management?
Many beginners in project management say that by studying PMP/IPMP and other related courses, they can systematically master the ten areas of project management and five process groups and other related knowledge points, but when they actually carry out project management work, they are still confused.
Many project managers often report the following problems: lack of awareness of project management, relying solely on personal experience, having only project management theory but not knowing how to practice; lack of systematic project management process and system support, unable to implement in work, inaccurate project estimation, poor control sensitivity, and project delays; unclear division of labor among members, and the "veterans" in the team do not know how to respond; cross-departmental assistance and communication are not smooth, and it is difficult to advance the project...
Therefore, Zhongtian Huaxia Consulting, which has focused on product innovation and R&D management for more than a decade, has helped many excellent enterprises to train a large number of key R&D talents such as product managers and project managers, and has won honorary titles such as "China Enterprise R&D Management Talent Training Demonstration Base". It has brought the online course "R&D Project Manager Special Training Camp".
The online course of "R&D Project Manager Special Training Camp" is an online fragmented learning method that combines many practical cases, tools and methods of R&D enterprises to help you master the essential knowledge and standard actions for project managers, and take your own project management to the next level.
It is also an opportunity for companies to promote the process of project manager training with lower costs and less investment, and bring high-efficiency operation results to companies.
Words are not enough to prove it. Let's take a look at how other students evaluate this course: This course is not only explained in depth and in simple terms by the expert team of Zhongtian Huaxia (the original Huawei R&D management team), but also combined with international advanced project management methodology and many real business scenarios of famous enterprises.
It will also provide scientific and practical management tools and methods, and rich template forms to help students convert and apply the learning content to specific work after class.
