Iranian President: Iran nuclear talks may reach an agreement if sanctions against Iran are lifted - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Tehran, December 11 (Reporters Gao Wencheng and Wang Shoubao) Iranian President Ebrahim Raisi said on the 11th in Tehran, the capital of Iran, that if the United States lifted its sanctions against Iran, the negotiations on the comprehensive agreement on Iran's nuclear issue could reach a "good agreement".
According to the news released by the Iranian President website, Larijani said in a meeting with the envoys of Iran in neighboring countries that Iran has proved its sincerity in negotiations by submitting proposals to other parties involved in the Iran nuclear agreement.
If the US is determined, "the road to reaching an agreement will be smooth".
The parties to the Iran nuclear deal began talks in April in Vienna, the capital of Austria, to discuss the resumption of the implementation of the agreement by the United States and Iran.
The new round of talks began in Vienna on November 29, and was temporarily adjourned on December 3, and resumed on December 9.
