The maximum length of time for Guangxi university students to take a break from school to start a business is five years - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Nanning, May 19 (Reporter Zhang Ying) -- The reporter learned from the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region Education Department that in the future, universities in Guangxi will implement flexible academic systems and relax the duration of students' leave of absence. The duration of students' leave of absence to start their own business can be extended by 2-5 years on the basis of the original academic system, and the time spent on leave of absence for starting a business can be regarded as practical education time.
In order to promote the improvement of college students' entrepreneurship and innovation ability, Guangxi Education, Human Resources and Social Security and other departments have jointly built an entrepreneurial platform, built more off-campus practice teaching bases for college students, university science parks, college students' business parks, business incubation bases, etc., and provided external guarantees for college students' entrepreneurship.
According to requirements, by 2020, the area of the innovation and entrepreneurship practice base of each university should reach more than 3,000 square meters for undergraduate schools and more than 2,000 square meters for vocational colleges.
The government encourages colleges and universities to establish innovation and entrepreneurship credits, and gives priority to supporting students who perform excellently in innovation and entrepreneurship practice to change their majors.
Every two years, teachers in colleges and universities should be seconded to industrial enterprises for at least two months to improve their awareness and ability in innovation and entrepreneurship education.
The Autonomous Region Education Department requires that all universities in Guangxi should deeply implement the training plan for college students’ innovation and entrepreneurship, and strive to make every student participate in an innovation and entrepreneurship training program during their school years.
Universities should actively organize students to participate in various types of entrepreneurship and innovation competitions at all levels, and provide financial support.
NEWS GOV-MO: UM Honours Seven Distinguished Persons with Honorary Doctorates
The University of Macau (UM) held the “2021 Conferment Ceremony of Honorary and Higher Degrees” today (11) to award the UM Honorary Doctorate degrees to Liu Zhongyi, Chen Kaiqian, Nakamura Shuji, Li Lanjuan, Li Xiaoliang, Zhu Lijuan and Jiang Chaohui, in recognition of their outstanding achievements and significant contributions to the development of society and education.
At the award ceremony, Chief Executive and representative of the University of Macau Council, Secretary for Social Affairs and Culture Ouyang Yu presented honorary doctorate degrees in the presence of President of the University of Macau Council, Lin Jin Cheng, and President of the University of Macau, Song Yonghua.
Professor Liu Zhongyi was awarded an honorary doctorate in education, Professor Chen Kai was awarded an honorary doctorate in science, Professor Shuji Nakamura was awarded an honorary doctorate in science, Professor Li Lanjuan was awarded an honorary doctorate in science, Professor Li Xiaoliang was awarded an honorary doctorate in business administration, Professor Zhu Lijuan was awarded an honorary doctorate in science, and Ms. Jiang Chao was awarded an honorary doctorate in science.
When delivering his speech, Ouyang Yu first extended warm congratulations and high respect to the seven outstanding individuals who were awarded honorary doctorates, as they have achieved remarkable accomplishments in different fields and made outstanding contributions to the development of the country and the progress of the world; he also expressed his most sincere blessings to graduates and parents, and paid heartfelt respects to the university’s teaching staff team who are devoted to their jobs and have excellent academic skills.
Sun Yifeng, a professor at the Faculty of Humanities at the University of Macau, read out the praises of Liu Zhenyi, saying that Professor Liu Zhenyi is a world-renowned economist, known for his outstanding academic achievements and forward-looking educational concepts.
In addition to his achievements in economic development, economic growth and East Asian economy, he was also a visionary educational leader.
In short, he has made outstanding contributions in many fields.
Sun Yifeng read the eulogy of Shuji Nakamura, saying that Professor Shuji Nakamura is a pioneer in sustainable energy technology.
He was one of three winners of the 2014 Nobel Prize in Physics for inventing blue light-emitting diodes (LEDs).
Professor Nakamura’s invention not only completely changed the lighting industry, but also promoted the production of white light-emitting diodes that are widely used in daily life and industrial production today, making a great contribution to human well-being.
When reading the praises of Li Lanjuan, Sun Yifeng said that Professor Li Lanjuan, as a pioneer of China’s artificial liver industry, has created a unique and effective Li-style artificial liver system, made significant breakthroughs in the treatment of severe hepatitis and hepatic failure, and significantly reduced the mortality rate of hepatic failure.
In this battle against COVID-19, her and her team’s “four resistances and two balances” plan as well as the artificial liver, microecology and stem cell technologies she brought significantly improved the critical care rate.
In his reading of Professor Li’s eulogy, Sun Yifeng said that Professor Li laid the foundation for innovative research in operations management, shaped the way of thinking in supply chain theory and practice, and completely changed business models around the world.
Li Xiaoliang is known for popularizing the concept of the long whip effect in operations management and has explored ways to deal with this phenomenon.
Today, under the epidemic and tense economic situation, the bullwhip effect is more prominent in various countries, causing serious damage to the supply chain.
Li Xiaoliang’s far-sighted research is like a ray of hope in the snow, helping the industry to cope with difficulties, and thus bringing about great social value.
When reading the praises of Zhu Li-lan, Sun Yifeng said that in her scientific research work, she discovered a breakthrough and innovative staining technique for sample preparation, which has a high reputation among domestic and foreign scientific peers.
She was honored with important honorary titles such as academician of the International Eurasian Academy of Sciences for her extraordinary scientific and technological achievements, and won the lofty status that she deserved in the world's science and technology temple with her brilliant achievements.
Chen Xin, Deputy Director of the Australian-Chinese Medical Research Institute, said in his reading of Chen Kexian’s tribute that Professor Chen Kexian has been engaged in drug research and development for more than 40 years, and his outstanding scientific achievements and important contributions to the country, Macao, the University of Macau, and key national laboratories have made him a respected international position and reputation.
His active role in promoting the development of traditional Chinese medicine in Macao and the Greater Bay Area fully reflects his sense of mission to contribute to the national medicine development strategy.
When Xu Chengzhong, Dean of the University of Macau Institute for Technology, read out Jiang Zhaohui’s eulogy, he said that Ms. Jiang Zhaohui’s major inventions and patents involved in research and development have accumulated more than 15 items related to storage virtualization, navigation, file systems and power management, which are highly practical, widely used, and improve the convenience of human life.
As an accomplished inventor, Ms. Jiang is often able to simplify complex science and theory and make them accessible to the public.
Finally, Chen Kai, as the representative of the honorary doctor, read the letter of thanks.
He was delighted to see that Macao and the Greater Bay Area have set a good example in the pharmaceutical industry: from the first State Key Laboratory of Quality Research in Traditional Chinese Medicine established by UM to the vigorous development of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area, UM has played a great role in integrating outstanding talents in the field of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area.
In addition, he believed that the management team of the University of Macau had far-sightedness, which not only provided fertile ground for students to conduct scientific research in academic terms, but also sent many responsible talents to society.
He was honored to be able to exchange and cooperate with the University of Macau, and he sincerely congratulated the University of Macau on its achievements in recent years.
