As NFTs quickly went viral, a new concept emerged in the crypto community.
In 2021, a blockchain game called Axie Infinity had a huge impact in Southeast Asia, and some residents who lost their jobs due to the pandemic began to earn stable income from this game.
Axie Infinity is a pet-raising game based on blockchain technology, which combines various gameplay, including NFT. It is currently the NFT project with the highest transaction volume, which has exceeded $3 billion.
Axie Infinity's daily revenue of more than $8.2 million is close to that of Honor of Kings, according to TokenTerminal data.
On August 6 this year, Axie Infinity officially announced that its daily active users had exceeded 1 million.
The popularity of Axie Infinity has brought a new “play-to-earn” model to more people. With the help of blockchain and smart contracts, players are no longer just characters. In addition to enjoying the game and earning economic benefits, they can also participate in the governance of the game ecology.
This subjectivity is not granted by the game producer, but is guaranteed by blockchain technology.
After seeing a news about the stock price of a friend, my biggest impression is the choice of the track of the enterprise, that is, the choice of the target industry. First, we should choose an industry with large growth space, at least with a market size of more than 100 billion; second, we should choose an industry with good future growth, considering the industry with the best growth in the next 3-5 years; finally, we should choose an industry with policy support.
The width of the track refers to the market size, the length of the track refers to the development stage of the industry, and the flatness or roughness of the track refers to the competitive landscape of the industry.
Cheer for the right track!
The first thing to do in the new year is to summarize 2021 and adjust the tactical layout of 2022.
The tactic is to "do the things right".
The strategy is to “do the right thing”.
The strategy lies in finding direction and the tactics lie in implementation. There is always room for strategic thinking above most tactical thinking.
For example, beyond how to increase customer numbers (tactical thinking), we can think about whether to continue to deepen in the current field or expand horizontally (strategic thinking); for example, beyond how to improve customer retention rate (tactical thinking), we can think about how to improve the retention rate of core customers and high-value customers (strategic thinking); beyond how to increase activity participation (tactical thinking), we can consider how to set the correct activity KPIs to achieve the correct activity goals, such as increasing target customer participation, activating high-value silent customers, and accurately attracting new customers; beyond how to increase DAU (tactical thinking), we can consider whether the current growth is healthy and sustainable.
After 12 years, Bitcoin has seen several milestone events in 2021.
On September 7, El Salvador, a small Central American country, designated Bitcoin as legal tender. This was the first time that Bitcoin had been designated as legal tender in a country or region.
On October 12, the US Securities and Exchange Commission approved ProShares to launch a Bitcoin ETF for the first time in eight years, and listed it on the New York Stock Exchange. This marked the first compliant Bitcoin futures ETF landing in the US capital market, and the further expansion of cryptocurrency investment exposure.
From the perspective of blockchain technology development, Bitcoin is not the main character.
On November 14, 2021, Bitcoin underwent a soft fork upgrade called "Taproot", which increased the anonymity of Bitcoin network transactions and reduced the data burden in transactions by changing the structure of blocks themselves.
