In September 2020, Mr. Lu learned from a real estate agent about a factory building in Zhangting Town, Yuyao, Zhejiang Province. After visiting the site several times, Mr. Lu decided to buy the factory building.
In December of the same year, Mr. Lu negotiated with Lin, a family member of the property owner, on the details of the purchase of the factory building, and transferred 200,000 yuan as a deposit through bank transfer on the same day.
Ling signed as the recipient in the "Factory Purchase Deposit Receipt", which stated, "If the buyer does not want to buy this factory, the deposit will belong to the seller. If the seller does not want to sell this factory, the deposit will be doubled and returned to the seller. Both parties agreed to sign a factory purchase contract within one week."
However, after that, both parties failed to reach an agreement on the main contract terms such as the scope of factory sale and payment method, which led to the delay in signing the house purchase contract.
Considering that both parties failed to reach an agreement on the contract content, Lin returned the 200,000 yuan deposit to Mr Lu a few days later.
After a lot of effort, Mr. Lu found a house he liked, paid the deposit, and prepared the house payment. All he needed was to sign the contract, but the seller refused to sell. This made Mr. Lu helpless and angry.
For this reason, Mr Lu sued Lin at the Yuyao City People's Court.
The court held that the failure of the two parties to sign a formal contract should not be attributed solely to the defendant, and it should be reasonably presumed that the negotiation failed. Therefore, the deposit penalty rule should not be applied in this case, and the defendant did not need to bear the liability for breach of contract of double return of the deposit.
After the first-instance judgment, the plaintiff filed an appeal.
Recently, the second-instance court upheld the original judgment.
[Lawyer's reminder] It is necessary to take due care in the transaction process.
When signing a contract, as a buyer, you should take necessary due diligence obligations, such as verifying the information of the house owner and whether the house is occupied, and clearly specify the specific time and place of delivery in the contract to prevent disputes between both parties when performing the contract.
(Sinica Deutsche Welle) After the "Democracy Summit" ended on Friday, a spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of China said in a statement on Saturday (December 11) that the United States held the "Leadership Summit for Democracy", which was "to draw ideological lines, to instrumentalize and weaponize democracy, to act against democracy in the name of democracy, to incite division and confrontation, and to divert domestic contradictions".
The Chinese government believes that “for a long time, the United States has forced its political system and values on others, promoted "democratic transformation", imposed unilateral sanctions, instigated "color revolutions", and caused catastrophic consequences.
'Democracy' has long been the 'weapon of mass destruction' used by the United States to interfere in other countries.
The summit is a move by Biden to deliver on his campaign promises.
The two-day meeting was held via video, and leaders of 111 countries around the world were invited to attend, including the leaders of Taiwan, but China and Russia were not invited.
On the eve of the summit, China and Russia criticized the United States for its own democratic problems, saying that the United States was not qualified to host such a summit.
There are also voices of doubt in the international community and within the United States, such as criticism that some leaders with authoritarian tendencies were invited to attend, such as leaders from the Philippines, Poland and Brazil. Some people suspect that the real intention of the Biden administration is not to organize this summit for democracy but for geopolitical purposes.
Newly appointed German Chancellor Scholz also attended the video democracy summit
The Chinese Foreign Ministry’s statement on Saturday said that “the pathological American democracy is fully displayed today, and the problems of money politics, identity politics, party opposition, political polarization, social tearing, racial contradictions, and rich-poor divide are becoming more and more severe”, and that the democracy in the United States is a “rich man’s game” built on the capital foundation.
U.S. President Biden said in his speech, "As leaders of government, we have a responsibility to listen to our citizens, strengthen the guardrails of democracy, promote reform, achieve transparent accountability governance, and be more resistant to the buffer and shock force of autocracy, as well as those who want to pursue power nakedly before the public interest. "
He stressed that democracy is not something taken for granted, "We must constantly renew it in every generation, and I believe this is the defining challenge of our time."
Biden also said that democracy and human rights around the world "face ongoing and worrying challenges," and that "democracy needs fighters to defend it."
The United States has promised to launch a year-long campaign after this democracy summit, including a $424.4 million initiative to strengthen democracy around the world and support independent media.
The United States hopes that countries will make specific public commitments to improve their democratic systems before the physical democracy summit planned for late 2022.
Biden said, "Let all of us implement our commitments and report on our progress next year."
