How to drink a red label whisky?
Everyone has different hobbies. Some people like collecting, some people like food, and of course, some people like wine. Red Label Whisky is one of the most popular Scotch Whiskies in various countries at present, and Red Label Whisky has won the gold medal in the International Spirits Competition.
Each bottle of Red Label whisky has its own unique taste, but it would be a waste to not know how to taste it.
So how do you drink Red Label whisky?
The editor will give you a brief introduction.
How to drink Red Label whisky:
Johnnie Walker Red Label is a blend of about 35 Scottish whiskies, with a rich aroma and traditional Scottish whisky characteristics, with sweet and smoky flavors in the rich aroma.
The entrance is rich and fresh, with a hint of vanilla and strong smoky malt.
It can be enjoyed on its own with ice or mixed with your favorite drink.
Red Label Whisky has entered the domestic market, and in order to adapt to the taste of the Chinese people, Red Label Whisky + Cola or Sprite or Fresca and other carbonated drinks have become a long-lasting fashion.
These sweet drinks, in addition to neutralizing the sour taste, can bring people pleasure visually. Adding them to drinks can dilute the alcohol and change the taste.
Red Label whisky + sliced lemon + cube sugar (or brown sugar) is the most authentic and traditional way to drink it.
The authentic red wine has a slightly sour taste, and sugar can neutralize its sourness. Lemon will give the wine a fresh fragrance. Of course, the sweetness and acidity can be adjusted according to personal taste.
The above three are the best ways to drink red label whiskey. You can try it as a reference. I hope my introduction can help you.
Educational Thinking: How can university exams meet the needs of "top students" and "underachievers"? - Xinhuanet
Three students from Lanzhou Jiaotong University wrote a letter to the school leaders, reflecting their confusion about the university exams and asking for an increase in the difficulty of the exams, changing the types of questions, and making the exams truly reflect the actual level of students.
Indeed, university exams have long been a "hot topic".
In a university campus, students come from all over the world, with different levels of ability, and with varying degrees of study, so the learning situation is very different.
It is inevitable that there will be different feelings when evaluating such a group with so many diverse characteristics.
Of course, if the exam questions are of a single type, with high repetition rates and too simple, it will inevitably cause a very different feeling.
Students who do not work hard may be able to pass the exam by cramming before the exam. If they try other methods, it is possible that they will achieve twice the result with half the effort.
As a result, there is a "strange situation" that "poor students" can pass and even get high scores without investment; "top students" never miss classes, do homework and take notes well, but don't get much higher scores in exams.
In this regard, the problems reflected by Lanzhou Jiaotong University students in the university examination are not without reason. It is believed that this situation does not exist only in Lanzhou Jiaotong University.
In this sense, we should applaud the three students who wrote the letter.
In fact, those who have attended university know that it is not uncommon to rush to prepare for exams and try every means to "extract" test questions from teachers, seek to define the scope of the exam, and seek "intensive guidance" before the exam. Even carrying cheat sheets in the examination and asking teachers to be lenient after the exam are not rare.
In the author’s view, as a teaching quality assessment guideline, the merit of a university’s exams is more dependent on the teacher’s overall grasp of teaching and learning, and the scientific formulation of questions based on this.
In the undergraduate stage, the majors begin to be subdivided, and many professional courses are based on basic knowledge.
Undoubtedly, whether a student has fully grasped the basic knowledge points of a subject is what university exams are designed to test.
Undergraduate knowledge is basically basic theory and common sense of disciplines, and there is not much room for change in terms of knowledge points, which are basically fixed.
As a teacher said, "The basic knowledge of college mathematics learned 20 years ago is still being studied now, and it is still the key point. "
However, the fact that the knowledge points remain basically unchanged does not mean that the exam questions are of a single type and the test questions are repeated.
In many universities, exams are generally composed of a group of examiners, and then compiled by senior teachers in charge of the subject, and the examination is also reviewed by all teachers responsible for the subject, which can overcome the problem of repeated questions to some extent.
However, to draw up a set of test questions that are in line with the actual situation of teaching and learning, the questions should be based on the overall situation of students' learning, and the difficulty should be normally distributed. It is also necessary to comprehensively master the teaching situation and comprehensively analyze the degree of students' learning, so that the examination proposition has dynamic control over the difficulty and question types, which can not only highlight the basic knowledge inspection, but also take into account the ability inspection, and at the same time innovate the question types.
Examinations are the baton of university education. Whatever kind of examinations there are, students will have corresponding preparation plans. In the long run, this will affect the effectiveness of university education.
Lanzhou Jiaotong University has attached great importance to the letter of advice from students and has deployed a rectification plan throughout the university.
It requires all teaching units to organize teachers to carry out discussions and self-examinations of course final exams, formulate examination papers and related systems, strengthen the supervision and inspection of examination paper proposition and review, refine the assessment of grades, and strengthen the comprehensive assessment of all links in course teaching.
Mechanically solving problems such as single question types and repeated questions is an issue that university examination affairs need to face. Of course, corresponding systems should be introduced, but the key lies in daily efforts. Teachers need to have a comprehensive grasp of teaching situations. They should not only thoroughly understand the teaching content, but also thoroughly understand the students' learning situation. With thorough understanding of both sides, teaching and learning will be better connected, forming a positive interaction, and the examination will be more in line with reality, so that "top students" and "poor students" can get what they deserve.
