Education news: Beijing reduces proportion of middle school entrance students with special talents in 2016 - Xinhuanet
On the 21st and 22nd, the Beijing Middle School Entrance Examination for Gifted Students was organized and implemented by the education commissions of each district.
This year, all districts in Beijing have reduced the proportion of students with special talents, and the competition for students with special talents has become more intense.
For example, in Dongcheng District, the proportion of students with special talents who entered middle school from primary school this year did not exceed 5% of the total number of students in the district. The number of students planned to be enrolled was 380, and the proportion of students who came to school did not exceed 10% of the number of students planned to be enrolled.
All students with special skills in sports, art and science who have registered online are eligible to participate in the examination for the admission of special talents.
In order to facilitate students to take the examination nearby, Dongcheng District continued last year's arrangement of the examination, and set up 1-2 examination sites in each school district, a total of 13 examination sites.
All examination points are divided into examination areas and divided into time periods in hours. On the day of the examination, students will enter the examination point at different examination areas according to the time period for examination.
On May 23, the list of students who passed the examination was published online by the District Education Admissions and Examination Center, and students could check their results online.
