48-hour negative nucleic acid test and "buffer zone" - State Council's joint prevention and control mechanism issues document to strengthen port city epidemic prevention and control - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 11 (Reporters Dong Ruifeng, Gu Tiancheng) The State Council's joint prevention and control mechanism recently issued a notice on strengthening the prevention and control of the COVID-19 epidemic in port cities, requiring people who recently left land border port cities (except those connected to Hong Kong and Macao) to hold negative nucleic acid test certificates within 48 hours, and people who went to land border port cities to undergo at least one nucleic acid test after arrival.
According to the notice, the above requirements apply from the date when the scope of port cities is determined and announced by each province, autonomous region or municipality, until March 15, 2022.
In addition, the notice also proposed that port cities with conditions may study setting up a buffer zone for epidemic prevention and control within their jurisdiction.
According to the relevant person in charge of the Disease Prevention and Control Bureau of the National Health Commission, for some port cities, cross-border border trade is the main economic pillar, and the border people of both sides come and go frequently.
Implementing a differentiated management policy for different regions, changing from one line of defense to two lines of defense, is expected to move the control points forward, compress the risk of epidemic overflow, and achieve the greatest effect in epidemic prevention and control with the least social impact and lowest social cost.
Recently, there have been several local cluster outbreaks in China, all of which were imported from overseas through port cities.
The above notice pointed out that this exposed some problems such as timely monitoring and early warning of epidemic in some places, non-implementation of closed-loop management for high-risk personnel, formalism of regular nucleic acid testing, inadequate disinfection of cold chain items at all links, irregular management of centralized isolation sites, and insufficient scientific and precise emergency response to the epidemic.
The notice requires that efforts should be made from nine aspects, including improving the port city epidemic prevention and control mechanism, improving the epidemic monitoring and early warning system, and implementing border control measures, to accelerate the completion of port city prevention and control shortfalls and weaknesses, and to do a good job in prevention and control work without relaxation, scientifically and accurately, and to tighten the defense line against imported diseases.
The notice stressed that all port cities should study and deploy epidemic prevention and control and people's livelihood protection work simultaneously, announce and open up people's livelihood protection hotlines, regularly investigate the supply and price of basic living materials, and promptly solve and actively respond to prominent issues reflected by the masses.
According to the notice, the port cities referred to include counties (cities, districts, banners) where open land, water and air ports are located, as well as the cities (prefectures, states, leagues) and municipalities where they are located. The specific scope will be determined by each province (autonomous region, municipality) according to the needs of epidemic prevention and control and announced in a timely manner.
