I accidentally came across an article that talks about why this client wants to have the logistics company in the bonded zone do the canning from a business perspective and a storage perspective. Although canning is considered deep processing and does not fall within the scope of the bonded logistics company's business operations, here is the text below which may explain why the client wanted to do so.
I went to many milk powder manufacturers and contacted many milk powder production lines.
In fact, the raw materials of bagged and canned milk powder are exactly the same, with no difference.
So you might ask: Why is the shelf life of a bag one year, while that of a can is two years or more?
Or ask again: why is there such a big price difference between canned and bagged products?
In fact, from this point of view, many consumers or mothers believe that this is because the raw materials are different, so the quality will be much better.
In fact, the raw materials are the same, but people think that the more expensive ones are better.
There are also consumers who have this mentality and after eating, they say that the taste or flavor of the canned food is different!
Now, I will first tell you why the price is so high. Why is it so expensive?
They are made of the same raw materials, so why is the price difference so large?
Because when manufacturers set prices, they mostly consider that if the bagged pricing is too high, consumers will find it hard to accept, which means that the profit of manufacturers is very low, or there is no profit. So how can manufacturers survive?
So they have a big jump in the pricing of their canned goods to protect their profit margins.
Therefore, most manufacturers are promoting canned products rather than bagged products.
And the manufacturers that you think of, they spend tens of millions or even hundreds of millions on advertising every year. Where does this money come from?
You can imagine.
As society develops, market promotion costs, such as shopping mall sales staff, shopping mall display costs, product gift costs, advertising costs, etc., are also increasing.
So each manufacturer is constantly increasing new products, and these are canned goods, and their prices are also constantly rising. In fact, this is a new product that has emerged with the increase in market costs.
The main purpose is to make more profits, but in fact, their raw material costs will not increase by more than 3 or 4 yuan.
There are also some brands that, in order to promote their products, will do anything to link up with hospital doctors and ask them to assist in promoting their products, taking a profit ranging from 30 yuan to 80 yuan from each bottle.
And China's relevant laws absolutely do not allow such methods of operation. In fact, this practice is to deceive consumers.
It is recommended that people buy milk powder in bags and put it into cans at home. This can save costs, and increase the preservation and sealing of milk powder. It will not affect children.
Also, don’t think that the shelf life of canned food is longer than that of bagged food. If the shelf life of canned food and bagged food is the same after opening, it is just that bagged food is not easy to preserve after opening, and is prone to moisture and deterioration.
