The resource of Qinghai Lake naked carp has increased by 0.71 million tons this year - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, Dec. 11 (Reporters Luo Xiaofei and Zhang Hongxiang) Reporters learned from the Qinghai Provincial Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs that the latest monitoring results showed that the reserves of Qinghai Lake nude carp increased by 0.71 million tons this year compared with the previous year, reaching 108,500 tons, and the accumulated increase was more than 40 times compared with the early stage of protection in 2002.
The Qinghai Lake naked carp, commonly known as “Qinghai Lake fish”, is a rare fish species unique to the Qinghai Lake, and plays a crucial role in maintaining the “water-fish-bird” ecological chain and biodiversity in the Qinghai Lake basin.
In the 1960s and 1970s, due to factors such as massive human hunting and the increasingly degraded environment of the spawning waters, the number of naked carp in Qinghai Lake decreased sharply. In 2002, the resource reserve of naked carp in Qinghai Lake was only 2,592 tons.
In 2004, the Qinghai Lake naked carp was listed as an endangered species in the Red List of Chinese Species.
Since 2003, Qinghai Province has implemented the ban on fishing in Qinghai Lake and its main rivers and tributaries, prohibiting any unit, collective or individual from fishing for naked carp in Qinghai Lake and its main rivers and tributaries, and prohibiting the sale of naked carp and its products.
Meanwhile, through artificial propagation and release, cleaning up the main rivers of Qinghai Lake, designing scientific and reasonable "fish passage" and other measures to continue to increase protection efforts, the resource reserves of naked carp in Qinghai Lake have increased year by year.
Yang Lin, deputy director of the Qinghai Provincial Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, said that as of now, nearly 180 million Qinghai Lake nude carp have been artificially bred and released, and the contribution rate to the recovery of Qinghai Lake nude carp resources is more than 23%.
The Sanjiangyuan region in Qinghai is an important ecological barrier and water conservation area in China and even Asia, while Qinghai Lake is a natural barrier and ecological function area to control the eastward spread of desertification in the west.
In order to protect the ecological environment of the Sanjiangyuan region and Qinghai Lake, protect aquatic wildlife, and maintain the biodiversity of the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, Qinghai has successively issued notices on the ban of fishing in key waters of the Yangtze River, Yellow River and Qinghai Lake since this year, and has established a comprehensive management system for the ban of fishing in "one river, one river and one lake".
