Is it electric leakage if feet are numb after soaking in a foot bath basin?
Choosing an appropriate foot bath can play a good foot therapy and health care role. Today, Guomei editor will answer this question to help friends.
As people’s awareness of health care has increased, foot bath basins have become increasingly popular among consumers. A large number of products with different grades have emerged in the market, ranging from more than 100 yuan to thousands of yuan, giving consumers a lot of choice.
According to relevant data, compared with traditional household appliances, health care appliances such as foot bath basins are selling well, but there is no specific industry standard for foot bath basins, so there are certain safety hazards.
"It's too dangerous to soak your feet in electrified water!"
Mr. Li told reporters that recently he bought a foot bath tub for his father as a birthday gift, but when his father took a bath, he felt numbness on his feet.
Mr. Li first thought that it was caused by the vibration function of the foot bath tub, but he did not expect that his father still felt numbness in his feet after turning off the vibration function.
Mr. Li tried the electric pen, and the pen was lit. Mr. Li was surprised to find that the water in the foot bath basin was electrically charged.
Later, he contacted the merchant, and the merchant's attitude was not bad. Although he returned the foot bath basin, Mr. Li still felt unhappy.
He found that there were no clear industry standards for the popular foot baths, including the maximum temperature, who they were suitable for and what materials were safe to use.
However, in general, foot bath basins do not have electricity problems, but it is not excluded that a small number of products are not strictly controlled at the time of leaving the factory.
Therefore, when purchasing, choose a split foot bath basin.
Water and electricity are separated, so there is no safety hazard.
You can test it with an electric pen at will.
The 13th Provincial Tea Expo opens - Video Headlines - Hunan Daily Online - Huasheng Online
Hunan Daily, December 10 (All-media reporter Zhang Shangwu, Hu Panpan, correspondent Liu Xiaoling, photographer Li Jian) - This morning, the 13th Hunan Tea Industry Expo and Xinhua Black Tea Promotion Conference were held at the Hunan International Convention and Exhibition Center to showcase the tea industry, innovate tea technology, promote tea culture, and accelerate the goal of a tea industry worth 100 billion yuan.
Hou Shunli, Vice President of the Council of the All-China Federation of Supply and Marketing Cooperatives, and Ye Hongzhuan, Vice Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Provincial People's Congress, attended the opening ceremony.
Professor Liu Zhonghua, an academician of the Chinese Academy of Engineering, made a grand recommendation at the opening ceremony: the source of red tea is in Xinhua, and the rise of red tea has injected new impetus into the "five-colored Hunan tea".
In recent years, the Provincial Party Committee and Provincial Government have supported the tea industry development, promoted the construction of a 100 billion yuan Hunan tea industry, and formed a "three provinces and four waters five-color tea" development pattern.
The tea industry in the province has increased innovation, and the main tea categories such as green tea, dark tea, and black tea have been successively promoted. The main tea-producing areas have promoted the integration of tea and tourism to drive the income increase of tea farmers.
The fortune wheel turns, and black tea is back in force.
According to tea experts in the province, after picking green tea, black tea and dark tea, tea farmers can earn income throughout the year, and the output value of tea gardens will rise sharply.
