Ding Zilin: To my friends.
I would like to express my sincere thanks to all my friends for the humanitarian assistance they have given me over the more than 30 years since the death of my relatives, especially the assistance that has never been interrupted since I made a humanitarian appeal to my friends at home and abroad in my own name in early 1994.
Now, most of the victims' parents have passed away, and the orphans have grown up and started their own families and careers.
It is your righteous deeds that help us, the victims, to get through the most difficult moments.
The coronavirus is currently raging around the world and most of the donors have retired.
Therefore, I sincerely request you to stop our relatives - the Tiananmen Mothers group from receiving humanitarian donations. This humanitarian rescue activity should have been brought to a perfect end long ago.
I will always remember your kindness and believe that your good deeds will be remembered in history.
For various reasons, I can only express my wishes in this way. Please forgive me!
Please accept my sincere best wishes.
Tao Yi: Please allow me to take this opportunity to make a brief introduction to the 32-year history of humanitarian relief of the International Federation of Chinese Students and Scholars (IFCSS) and the Minnesota China Democracy Foundation (MCDF).
In the process of humanitarian assistance, the All-American Students Union and the Minnesota China Democracy Foundation are two parallel organizations, and the project executors often intersect.
(Apple Daily photo: Tiananmen Mothers website is managed by Tao Yi.) pic.twitter.com/UxID9ZGjzm
Relief funds often fail to reach the hands of the victims of June 4th.
In 1994, at the suggestion of Teacher Ding, a special group was established by the "Tiananmen Mothers" to coordinate and be responsible for the reception and distribution of humanitarian relief funds.
In 1998, the MCDF established the "June 4 Orphan Education Fund". After 11 years of implementation, in 2009, after all the June 4 orphans graduated from university, the MCDF then established the "June 4 Orphan and Elderly Poor Relief Fund", which has been implemented to this day.
The funding for these projects comes mainly from campus and community donations from the year of the Tiananmen Square massacre, generous donations from individuals, and support from the Foundation for Democracy at Sister Universities.
Since 2018, it has also been supported by the Prison Studies Foundation.
Last year, after 31 years, the victims of June 4 finally received a portion of the donations collected in the name of June 4 from Hong Kong.
During this period, China Human Rights was also independently implementing its humanitarian assistance projects.
We understand that Mr. Ding stopped the June 4th donation for the sake of the donors. We are indeed some retired people and our income is not as abundant as before retirement. We hereby express our gratitude to Mr. Ding’s letter “To Friends”.
We will respect the decision of the survivors and end the project within two years, and resume it immediately if needed.
I would like to express my gratitude and respect to those brave comrades who have been generous and risked their lives to deliver humanitarian aid for years.
