A beginner programmer who wants to share his personal experience.
If you are planning to enter this industry, you can choose to go to a place for training, but if you have no such idea, it is better to learn by yourself. After all, the cost of training is very high, and you have to spend 6 months to learn.
But if you want to get into this industry, training is definitely a good choice, especially for those who have weak self-control, training is an even better choice.
If you have strong self-control, you can also choose to learn on your own, but it will be more tiring.
Of course, choosing a good training institution is very important.
First, we should look at the teaching staff of this institution. If the teaching staff is not strong enough, then this training institution will be meaningless. Of course, some newly opened training institutions do not have a very strong teaching staff.
Secondly, before making a choice, you should inquire about the training institution. It is best to inquire about the students who have graduated from this institution. After all, only the students of this institution can tell you how good or bad the courses are.
Hello, I don't really know how to answer your question, because you haven't given me any information about your own situation. Learning this stuff is very much related to your own personal situation.
For example, your specialty, age, the language you want to learn, and even the city you are in, all of these things are related to the industry you are studying or want to work in.
If you are a student and have not graduated yet, or if you are a computer major and have graduated, then I personally recommend self-study if you have enough time. This is the most efficient and cost-effective method. Many offline and online training institutions are actually very good, but the cost of learning is high, and the time investment is relatively large. Basically, you need to concentrate on training for 3-6 months.
But if it is what I said, self-study is very convenient. There are many free learning resources on the Internet now, or you can also find many training resources on Bilibili. If you don't know how to find resources, you can also contact me through a brief introduction to get free resources, or detailed consultation.
There are also some classic books that can be combined with video to provide a comprehensive learning experience.
If you are not a computer professional, but can afford to pay for the cost of learning and time, it is recommended to go to a training institution to study. This way, you will not have to work hard, the teacher will explain in detail, and there will be someone to answer your questions. In addition, it will also help with learning planning or supervision.
Moreover, many training institutions will sign employment agreements and have internal referral quotas. After learning, they will recommend students to companies, which can save a lot of time in the interview process for future job hunting.
These are some of my views. As I said earlier, I don’t know your situation, so I haven’t explained it in detail. If you have any other questions, you can contact me at any time for communication and exchange.
