Chinese and Saudi curators team up to hold Saudi Arabia's first contemporary art biennale - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Riyadh, Dec. 12 (Reporters Wang Haihou and Hu Guan) The first contemporary art biennale in Saudi Arabia, Diriyah Contemporary Art Biennale, was officially opened to the public on December 11 at the JAX Art District in Diriyah, northwest of the Saudi capital Riyadh. A total of 64 artists from Saudi Arabia, China and other places participated in the exhibition.
This biennale was jointly organized by the Saudi Diriyah Biennial Foundation and the UCCA Center for Contemporary Art in China, with Tian Fei-yu, director of the UCCA Center for Contemporary Art in China, serving as artistic director.
According to the curatorial team, the theme of this biennial is "crossing the river by feeling the stones", which metaphorically refers to the reform strategies adopted during the period of socio-economic transformation and reflects the current situation of Saudi social and cultural development.
The biennial covers an area of nearly 12,000 square meters, and the exhibition hall spans six interconnected buildings, which are presented in six units: "Crossing the River by Touching Stones", "Inheritance as Experiment", "Thinking at the Edge", "Towards the Public", "A Beautiful New World" and "On the Spirit of Art".
Among them, the works of 27 Saudi artists account for more than 40% of the total number of exhibits, covering painting, installation art and performance art; the works of 12 Chinese artists have also attracted great attention, some artists use recycled materials in new ways to create works, such as Xu Bing’s “Behind the Story Series: Stream and Mountains Without End” (2014), which reconstitutes a classic landscape painting with waste.
Buckley, CEO of the Diriyah Biennale Foundation, said that he hoped that this biennale would establish an international dialogue, giving global audiences the opportunity to learn about Saudi Arabia's booming cultural industry and creative community, and strengthen interaction.
Tian Feiyu said, "The goal of the Biennale is twofold, to allow Saudi contemporary art to participate in global dialogue and to allow Saudi audiences to be integrated into the world of contemporary art. "
It is understood that a series of lectures will also be held during the opening period of the biennale, and artists, curators and creative industry opinion leaders will discuss topics such as cross-cultural exchange and contemporary art development.
