Yunnan: Coordinate and standardize the management of rural public welfare posts - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Kunming, December 12 (Reporter Lin Bifeng) In order to continue to do a good job in employment assistance for poverty-stricken people and consolidate and expand the achievements of poverty eradication, Yunnan Province recently issued relevant policies on promoting the management of rural public welfare positions to help comprehensively promote rural revitalization.
According to relevant officials of the Yunnan Provincial Human Resources and Social Security Department, at present, Yunnan has developed 448,300 rural public welfare positions for the placement of poverty-stricken labor force and other rural disadvantaged groups, which have played an important role in helping the poor people achieve employment and income increase, consolidating the achievements of poverty alleviation, and effectively enhancing the public service capabilities of villages.
This new regulation was jointly issued by seven departments in Yunnan Province, including the Human Resources and Social Security Bureau, Rural Revitalization Bureau, and Finance Bureau. It mainly standardizes the scope of recruitment for village-level public welfare positions, fund management, position development, and position management.
In terms of post development and placement, the new rules clearly stipulate that the posts should be set up according to the principles of “setting up posts according to needs, assigning people according to posts, dynamic management, total quantity control”, “whoever develops the post, uses it and is responsible for it”, and “one person, one post, voluntary publicity, unified management”.
The recruitment process must be carried out in accordance with the announcement, declaration, examination, public display, employment, pre-job training and job assignment steps.
In addition, the new rules also clarify the specific duties of the main departments for developing rural public welfare positions, the subsidy standards and methods for rural public welfare positions, and stipulate that each department responsible for developing rural public welfare positions should purchase commercial insurance for the placement personnel in rural public welfare positions; and require relevant departments to regularly supervise the distribution of subsidies for rural public welfare positions.
