Let's take a look at some of the [weird trending topics] today.
What is normal public opinion?
Three hot topics are randomly selected: the Dragon Dance on February 2, the price hike of Hualiyou, and the Gulala incident. The public opinion spreads and forms a wave peak, and then the [index falls] (smooth curve) finally disappears. If there is a secondary public opinion, a small hump will appear again.
They look no different from the [evolutionary model of online public opinion] once displayed on the official website of the Cyberspace Administration of China.
What is an abnormal public opinion?
Six hot searches were randomly selected from the same event, and presented in a [peak-like], [sawtooth-like] and [cliff-like] manner.
The “solitary peak” means that it is artificially heated, quickly surges to the hot search list, and attracts public attention; the “sawtooth” means that it is periodically heated to ensure that the topic stays on the hot search list; the “cliff” means that it is collectively withdrawn, and after the hot search has played its “function”, it receives a new task and rushes to a new battlefield.
In Figure 9, the peak of one event's popularity coincides with the trough of another event's popularity, and the time is precise. This must be due to a unified batch of water army receiving a task and starting a new offensive.
The professionalism of black PR is evident: dozens of hot search topics are listed at the same time. Which ones attract attention, which ones are responsible for science popularization, which ones start a war, which ones divert attention, which ones affect cognition, which ones mislead judgment, which ones incite emotions, and which ones entrap decisions. Black production accounts are finely divided into batches and nodes, and almost all elements in the spread of public opinion are considered.
Communication is a science. If we leave aside all subjective factors such as position and emotion, and only consider objective data, black PR will have no place to hide.
Every step leaves a trace. We will dig out these traces together.
Data source: Hot Search Time Machine.
Mauritius and other countries first found Omicron strain infection cases - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 12 -- According to the comprehensive reports of Xinhua News Agency correspondents stationed abroad: Mauritius, Cyprus and Malawi have reported for the first time the discovery of cases infected with the Omicron variant of coronavirus.
Mauritius reported its first two cases of Omicron infection on October 10.
According to Kailash Jagtap, the Minister of Health in Mauritius, one infected person is a tourist who arrived in Mauritius on November 27 from South Africa; another infected person is a local resident in Mauritius, he was in contact with a person who had recently gone to South Africa and returned, and tested positive for nucleic acid test on November 30.
After hospital isolation treatment, the nucleic acid test results of these two infected persons turned negative and they have returned to their respective places of residence.
The Cypriot Ministry of Health announced on the 10th that it had confirmed three cases of Omicron infection for the first time in the country.
All three were students who had returned from a trip abroad earlier this month, and did not require hospitalization as their symptoms were mild.
In order to prevent the spread of Omicron, the government has continuously increased its efforts to control the epidemic.
From December 6 to January 10 next year, passengers aged 12 and above who arrive in the country by air will be required to undergo nucleic acid testing at the airport at their own expense.
On the 10th day of the month, the Ministry of Health also announced that it would begin to vaccinate children aged 5 to 11 in the country with Pfizer's coronavirus vaccine.
Kumbize Chiponda, the Minister of Health of Malawi, said on the 9th that the country had found three cases of infection with the Omicron strain for the first time.
The country's health department found these three cases after conducting genome sequencing on 12 positive samples collected from November 9 to December 2.
