I'm sorry, but as a woman I can't just sit back and be silent any longer.
You have not stopped at all, but have grown more arrogant after my news of calling the police was uploaded.
I don't care what your political background is or what your status is, in our society we need respect for both genders.
Yes, you can continue to make these snarky, veiled, humiliating, and abusive comments, you can continue to say that you just care about me, you can continue to think that this isn't harassment, you can even continue to deny that you made those images or continue to spew all of your hate.
Yes, I can't and I don't have the power to stop you.
I don't know you and I don't want to know you, and I don't need you to judge me on my looks or my body.
I don't even think there's a girl out there who would be willing to be so humiliated in order to get famous.
My friends asked me if I was okay.
I said yes, and you wouldn't believe it.
I don't think any girl could say she was okay after being bullied like that.
In the workplace, in society, in politics or in business, only those who lack basic decency would choose to harm any woman in this way.
I believe that justice is in the hearts of people.
I have selected some comments for you to read.
You posted it yourself, so no one can impersonate you
I can only say that you are the enemy of civilization.
A smile of recognition
Vietnam News Online - Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh attended the Third Vietnam National Digital Technology Enterprise Development Forum
Two major meetings were held during the third Vietnam National Digital Technology Enterprise Development Forum, with topics focusing on digital technology enterprises and national digital transformation, as well as digital technology enterprises and economic recovery and development after the pandemic.
According to Minister of Information and Communications Nguyen Benh Xuan, in 2021, despite the continued spread of COVID-19, the number of digital technology enterprises and revenue in Vietnam still maintained growth momentum at nearly 10%.
In 2021, Vietnam will cultivate a number of typical digital products to solve the major problems faced by Vietnam. Many digital products have gone overseas, and Vietnam's digital technology ranking has improved.
Minister Ruan Mengxiong called on digital technology companies to take responsibility for developing the country's digital transformation platform, and taking on the task of developing these national digital platforms is a national mission.
At the forum, leaders of various departments and state organs, enterprises, organizations, and individuals that are researching, developing, applying, and transferring digital technologies shared their breakthrough ideas and solutions for mobilizing and pooling resources from all sectors of society to develop Vietnamese technology enterprises, jointly promote national digital transformation, and revive the economy after the epidemic.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh stressed in his speech at the forum that digital transformation is an inevitable path for the world and an objective demand for development.
Digital transformation has become a global issue, and digital transformation services all people, so it is necessary to mobilize all people to participate.
People and enterprises are the core, main body, goal and driving force of digital transformation.
Therefore, all policies must be for the people and businesses.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng stressed that digital transformation should reflect the national spirit, and should be based on internal forces, strategy, long-term and decisive factors, and external forces as important and breakthrough points.
He also believed that digital transformation should drive in-depth and sustainable development, participate in the prevention and control of the COVID-19 epidemic, economic recovery and development, cope with subsequent changes, overcome the depletion of natural resources, and help green transformation and the development of green energy.
Digital transformation requires participation in the establishment of databases for protecting and promoting national cultural values, historical traditions, and national customs and habits, as well as the promotion of digital transformation in banks, tax, land management and development databases, logistics, and other fields.
The ultimate goal of digital transformation is to make people happier and the country more prosperous.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh requested that all levels of government, agencies and enterprises should increase leadership and guidance in developing digital technology, raise awareness of digital transformation, continue to formulate and improve systems on digital transformation, strengthen national management, and promote the development of digital technology enterprises with respect, communication, listening, positive and proactive spirit.
During the forum, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh attended the award ceremony of the 2021 “Made in Vietnam” Excellent Digital Product Award and the opening ceremony of the “Made in Vietnam” Digital Product Exhibition.
