The Yangtze River Main Channel Achieves Full Coverage of Water-based Green Comprehensive Service Areas - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Wuhan, December 11 (Reporter Wang Xian) The Chongqing Fuling Water Green Comprehensive Service Area was completed and put into operation as scheduled on December 10. This is the second water green comprehensive service area officially put into operation in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River after the Sichuan Luzhou Water Green Comprehensive Service Area was put into operation on December 8.
Up to now, the water-based green comprehensive service area has covered the upper, middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River.
Qiu Jianhua, deputy director of the Yangtze River Shipping Administration Bureau of the Ministry of Transport, said that previously, Hubei, Hunan, Jiangxi, Anhui, Jiangsu and other provinces have built and operated 10 water-based green integrated service areas in the middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River, which have been recognized by the majority of sailors and played an important role in promoting the high-quality development of Yangtze River shipping.
The full coverage of green comprehensive service areas on water is another milestone event in the construction of green shipping on the Yangtze River, and the reception of ship pollutants and shipping services on the Yangtze River have been significantly improved.
It is reported that the water-based green comprehensive service area provides all-round production and living services for ships and crew members, and helps to solve the "urgent, difficult, anxious and worried" problems of the vast majority of crew members.
The two water-based green comprehensive service areas built and put into operation in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River integrate living services, production services and government services, and are themed on green environmental protection, with ship maintenance and ship emergency rescue services as their characteristics. They realize the "one-time berthing, multiple services" for ships in the port, and will make the work of crew members who sail the Yangtze River year-round more efficient and their lives more convenient.
Three US aircraft carriers gather around China, the most powerful weapon rarely visits Guam 2022-01-17 DW The latest news on Sino-US relations: The latest satellite images show that three US aircraft carriers are gathering around China; the US media also disclosed that one of the most powerful weapons in the US Navy's arsenal rarely visited Guam, sending an important signal to the allies and enemies of the United States in the Indo-Pacific region.
According to the Chinese think tank "South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception Platform", on January 9, the satellite found the US Navy's USS Carl Vinson aircraft carrier near the Balabac Strait.
The Balabac Strait connects the South China Sea and Sulu Sea, and is a strategic location on the first island chain in the western Pacific Ocean.
The platform predicted that the USS Carl Vinson would be deployed to the South China Sea.
This is the first time that the "Carl Vinson" aircraft carrier has deployed with F-35C fighter jets and CMV-22 Osprey amphibious transport aircraft.
In addition to the Carl Vinson, the US aircraft carrier that is currently cruising in the Pacific Ocean is the USS Abraham Lincoln, which departed from the United States on January 3.
The USS Lincoln also carried the F-35C squadron for the first time, which belongs to the 314th Fighter Attack Squadron of the US Marine Corps.
In addition to the above two aircraft carriers, the US Navy currently has the USS Ronald Reagan aircraft carrier, which is docked in Yokosuka, Japan, deployed in the Asia-Pacific region.
The aircraft carrier battle group also includes the missile cruiser "Champlain Lake" and the missile destroyer "Stockdale".
Three U.S. aircraft carriers gather near China, and the most powerful weapon makes rare visit to Guam. On January 17, 2022, the "South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception Platform" released the latest satellite images showing that three U.S. aircraft carriers were gathering near China.
(Weibo @South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception) The U.S. Navy's three aircraft carriers have gathered in the vicinity of China, and the most powerful weapon has made a rare visit to Guam. On January 17, 2022, the flight route of the U.S. Navy's carrier-based transport aircraft CMV-22B.
(Weibo @South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception) CNN reported on January 17 that one of the most powerful weapons in the U.S. Navy arsenal made an unusual visit to Guam last weekend.
The Ohio-class nuclear submarine USS Nevada, carrying 20 Trident ballistic missiles and dozens of nuclear warheads, entered the U.S. Navy base in Guam on Saturday (January 15).
The three US aircraft carriers gathered around China, and the most powerful weapon made a rare visit to Guam. According to analysts, this is a signal sent to allies and enemies in the increasingly tense situation in the Indian-Pacific region.
This is the first time that a U.S. ballistic missile submarine has visited Guam since 2016, and it is the second time that it has been publicly visited since the 1980s.
Three US aircraft carriers gather around China. The most powerful weapons rarely visit Guam. China has built a large number of military facilities in the Nansha Islands in recent years.
This is Yongshu Island in the South China Sea.
(South China Sea Research Forum) The US Navy said in a statement that the visit of the Ohio-class nuclear submarine "Nevada" to Guam strengthened the cooperation between the United States and its allies in the region, showed the ability, flexibility, and combat readiness of the United States, and its continued commitment to the security and stability of the Indo-Pacific region.
Ballistic missile submarines are commonly referred to as "Boomer" submarines.
The whereabouts of 14 "thundering submarines" in the U.S. Navy fleet is usually kept strictly confidential.
The secret surrounding ballistic missile submarines made the "thunder submarine" the most important survival weapon in the "nuclear triad", which also includes intercontinental ballistic missiles based on American soil and bombers such as B-2 and B-52 that can carry nuclear warheads.
Why did Meta's share price fall by 26% and its market value evaporate by $251 billion? Zuckerberg responded that "we face unprecedented competition."
Meta (formerly Facebook) is essentially an advertising company, and its income mainly comes from advertising. Today's advertising companies that make money have their own traffic channels.
Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp and so on, whatever their feature orientation, are Meta's traffic channels.
Moreover, Meta is also the largest “ad alliance”. Many apps connect to Meta’s ads and monetize through Meta’s ad platform.
But times have changed.
First, because of the adjustment of Apple's privacy policy, Meta has difficulty in obtaining user data information, which affects the efficiency of advertising.
Apple's current privacy policy is user-friendly and will clearly prompt users whether they allow apps to access their information. Most people's normal reaction would be not to allow it.
If Google pulls another stunt, the impact on Meta's revenue could be even greater.
Second, the China factor in Meta’s previous revenue growth has also weakened (the proportion of this factor is uncertain, but it does exist).
Everyone knows that Meta has no business in China, but this understanding is not accurate.
At least 10% of Meta's revenue comes from China each year, mainly from companies that do business in China.
Meta has several hundred employees in its Hong Kong office and several major agents on the mainland.
Meta is an advertising channel that Chinese companies cannot bypass when they want to expand overseas markets, and most of the money they spend goes to Meta.
Interestingly, Byte's TT is now one of Meta's main competitors, but two years ago Meta made a lot of money from Byte.
All domestic agents are helping ByteDance to place advertisements on Meta, and Meta’s performance in Greater China is also very good.
I haven't really looked at it recently but I don't think it's going to be any better than before.
The era of large-scale spending by Chinese companies overseas has passed.
Third, new traffic channels are not expanding smoothly.
Facebook is getting older and new platforms like TT aren't in Meta's hands.
The biggest problem is not just the decline in income, but the lack of growth expectations.
The capital market is not only concerned with income, but more importantly, it looks at how the future expectations are.
Clearly, Meta's expectations were not enough.
In order to tell a new story to the market, Zuckerberg talked about the "metaverse".
The metaverse is indeed one of the future directions, but the implementation cycle of the metaverse is relatively long, and this story should not be enough to support Meta’s market value in the next two or three years.
So the next two years should be a difficult period for Meta.
Although Facebook is now very successful and has annual revenues of $100 billion to $200 billion, it actually feels very threatened at present. Compared with other Internet companies and high-tech companies, Facebook does not have any good security moat.
Although several of his social software have a high number of daily active users and are mainstream social software, such as Facebook, WhatsApp, etc., Facebook is not confident in the face of the rapid development of TikTok. It only takes a blink of an eye to be disrupted.
And the Metaverse, this unattainable concept, has no chance of success in the short term. So Facebook is very dangerous. This is also the reason why Zuckerberg changed the company’s name and kept looking for new tracks. But I think his track selection is wrong, it is a dead end. The above is some of my thoughts for reference.
Article 17 The state shall implement a registration and practice management system for registered fire engineers.
Those who have obtained the first and second level registered fire engineer qualification certificates may practice in the name of registered fire engineers at the corresponding level after registration.
Article 18 The Fire Protection Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security is the registration and approval department for first-level registered fire engineers.
The fire protection agencies of the public security organs in provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government are the registration approval departments for the qualification of Level II registered fire engineers, and are responsible for the preliminary examination of the registration of Level I registered fire engineers.
Article 19 Persons who have obtained the qualification certificates of first-class and second-class registered fire engineers and apply for registration shall be employed by an approved fire technical service institution or a key fire safety unit, and submit the registration application materials to the fire protection agency of the public security organ at the location of the unit (if the employing unit is an enterprise, submit it to the industrial and commercial registration location through the enterprise).
Article 20 After receiving the registration application materials of the applicant, the fire protection agency of the public security organ of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government shall, if the application materials are incomplete or do not conform to the legal form, inform the applicant of all the content that needs to be corrected on the spot or within five working days. If it fails to inform the applicant after the expiration of the time limit, the application shall be accepted from the date of receipt of the application materials.
For registration applications accepted or not accepted, a written certificate with the special seal of the fire department of the public security organ at the corresponding level and the date shall be issued.
Article 21 The provincial, autonomous region and municipal public security fire institutions shall complete the preliminary review work of the first-level registered fire engineer qualification registration application materials and the registration approval work of the second-level registered fire engineer qualification within 20 working days from the date of acceptance of the registration application in accordance with the prescribed conditions and procedures, and report the first-level registered fire engineer qualification registration application materials and preliminary review opinions to the Fire Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security for approval.
The Fire Department of the Ministry of Public Security shall make a decision on whether to approve within 20 working days from the date of receiving the application materials and preliminary examination opinions submitted by the fire departments of provincial public security organs.
If the approval decision cannot be made within the prescribed period, the applicant shall be informed of the extended period and the reasons.
If a decision is made not to approve, the reasons shall be stated in writing and the applicant shall be informed of his/her right to apply for administrative reconsideration or initiate an administrative lawsuit according to law.
Article 22 The registration approval department shall issue and deliver the corresponding level of registration certificate within 10 working days from the date of making the approval decision.
Article 23 Each registration certificate shall be valid for three years.
The registration certificate is the practice credential of the corresponding level registered fire engineer during its validity period, and shall be kept and used by the registered fire engineer himself.
Article 24: Those who apply for initial registration shall submit their application within one year from the date of obtaining the qualification certificate of first and second level registered fire engineers.
When applying for initial registration after the deadline, the continuing education requirements of these regulations must be met.
Specific measures for registration management, such as initial registration, renewal registration, change registration, cancellation registration and non-registration shall be separately stipulated by the Ministry of Public Security.
Article 25 Continuing education is a necessary condition for the continuation registration, re-registration and overdue initial registration of registered fire engineers.
During each registration period, registered fire engineers at all levels shall complete corresponding continuing education in accordance with regulations.
Article 26 The registration approval department shall promptly announce to the public the relevant circumstances of the registration of registered fire protection engineers and establish an integrity file for registered fire protection engineers to implement credit management on their professional activities.
Article 27 The registration management department of registered fire engineers at all levels shall strictly implement the relevant provisions of the Administrative Licensing Law of the People's Republic of China.
That's all for today's exam information sharing. I hope it can help everyone.
Everyone must work hard to prepare for the exam and strive to pass the fire engineer examination as soon as possible!
