The "Peaceful Rescue-2021" joint military medical service exercise between the armies of China and Vietnam has been successfully concluded - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Hanoi, December 12 (reported by Zhou Na and Teng Weijin) -- On the morning of December 12, the Chinese contingent participating in the "Peaceful Rescue-2021" military medical service joint exercise with the Vietnamese army returned safely to Guangxi, China, marking the successful completion of the seven-day training mission.
In this joint exercise, the two armies of China and Vietnam focused on the major topic of humanitarian medical rescue, closely adhered to the mission of logistics and rescue, and completed the contents of joint logistics command, joint on-site rescue, and mass casualty treatment according to the standard of real combat, effectively improving the logistics support capabilities of the two armies.
The results of the exercise were affirmed by both the Chinese and Vietnamese armies.
Ruan Xiongsheng, Director of the Steering Committee for the Vietnamese military exercise, Deputy Director and Chief of Staff of the General Logistics Department of the Vietnamese People's Army, said at the ceremony that ended the exercise that through this exercise, the Vietnamese military doctors learned knowledge about the organization of the exercise and professional activities from the Chinese military doctors, and also saw the medical and support equipment of China.
The results of the exercise proved the professional ability of the two countries' medical forces in medical assistance and epidemic prevention and control.
Chen Chunming, head of the Guidance and Coordination Group and deputy director of the Health Bureau of the General Logistics Department of the Central Military Commission, said that this exercise was another innovative practice based on the successful holding of joint medical clinics in 2018, and had a very important milestone significance.
During the exercise, the People's Liberation Army of China donated medical protective masks, medical protective clothing, rapid nucleic acid testing instruments and other health and epidemic prevention materials to the Vietnamese People's Army.
